<%- include('partials/head', { title: 'How Nodevents works' }) %>
<section class="learning-hero">
  <p class="eyebrow">Nodevents learning center</p>
  <h1>Get everyone on<br>the same timeline.</h1>
  <p class="intro">A quick guide to planning an event, inviting vendors, sharing updates, and keeping invoices organized.</p>
  <a class="button primary" href="<%= user ? '/dashboard' : '/auth' %>"><%= user ? 'Open your dashboard' : 'Start planning' %> <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
</section>

<nav class="learning-nav" aria-label="Learning page sections">
  <a href="#overview">The idea</a>
  <a href="#planner">For planners</a>
  <a href="#vendors">For vendors</a>
  <a href="#live-updates">Live updates</a>
  <a href="#invoices">Invoices</a>
</nav>

<section class="learning-section" id="overview">
  <div class="learning-section-heading">
    <span class="learning-number">01</span>
    <div><p class="eyebrow">The idea</p><h2>One calm place for event coordination</h2></div>
  </div>
  <p class="learning-copy">Event details often end up split between chat threads, email, and spreadsheets. Nodevents brings the schedule, vendor responses, updates, and invoices together for the planner and gives each vendor a simple personal link.</p>
  <div class="learning-points">
    <article><h3>A shared schedule</h3><p>Keep vendor arrival times and event tasks in one timeline.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Clear responses</h3><p>See who confirmed, declined, or needs a change.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Fewer loose ends</h3><p>Track submitted invoices and whether they are approved or paid.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="learning-section" id="planner">
  <div class="learning-section-heading">
    <span class="learning-number">02</span>
    <div><p class="eyebrow">For planners</p><h2>Set up your event in a few steps</h2></div>
  </div>
  <ol class="learning-steps">
    <li><span>1</span><div><h3>Create your planner account</h3><p>Register with your name, email, and password, then sign in to your dashboard.</p></div></li>
    <li><span>2</span><div><h3>Create an event</h3><p>Add the event name, date, and venue. You can open an event later from the dashboard.</p></div></li>
    <li><span>3</span><div><h3>Add vendors</h3><p>Enter each vendor’s name and optional category and email. Nodevents creates a unique link for each vendor.</p></div></li>
    <li><span>4</span><div><h3>Build the timeline</h3><p>Add tasks with a date and time, then assign them to a vendor or mark them as event-wide. Save a new time whenever the schedule changes.</p></div></li>
    <li><span>5</span><div><h3>Watch confirmations and invoices</h3><p>The event page shows outstanding confirmations, vendor notes, submitted invoices, and recent changes.</p></div></li>
  </ol>
</section>

<section class="learning-section" id="vendors">
  <div class="learning-section-heading">
    <span class="learning-number">03</span>
    <div><p class="eyebrow">For vendors</p><h2>Open an invite or sign in to your account</h2></div>
  </div>
  <div class="learning-two-column">
    <div>
      <p class="learning-copy">Open the unique link from your planner to view event details and relevant timeline tasks, respond, or submit an invoice. From that invitation, you can create an account with the invited email address. Later, sign in to see all invitations you have linked to your account.</p>
      <ul class="learning-checklist">
        <li>Choose <strong>Confirm</strong>, <strong>Need changes</strong>, or <strong>Decline</strong>.</li>
        <li>Add a short note to explain a request or response.</li>
        <li>Use <a href="/vendor/login">vendor sign in</a> to return to your linked events.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <aside class="learning-callout"><strong>Keep your link private</strong><p>Anyone with a vendor link can see that vendor’s event details and respond on their behalf. Only share it directly with the intended vendor.</p></aside>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="learning-section" id="live-updates">
  <div class="learning-section-heading">
    <span class="learning-number">04</span>
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Live updates</p><h2>Changes reach the right people</h2></div>
  </div>
  <p class="learning-copy">When a planner adds a timeline task or changes its time, connected planner and vendor pages receive a live notification. When a vendor responds or sends an invoice, the planner is notified too. Select <strong>Refresh</strong> in the update banner to reload the latest page details.</p>
</section>

<section class="learning-section" id="invoices">
  <div class="learning-section-heading">
    <span class="learning-number">05</span>
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Invoice tracking</p><h2>Follow an invoice from sent to paid</h2></div>
  </div>
  <div class="invoice-flow" aria-label="Invoice progress">
    <span><strong>1</strong> Vendor sends an invoice</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    <span><strong>2</strong> Planner approves it</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    <span><strong>3</strong> Planner marks it paid</span>
  </div>
  <p class="learning-copy">Vendors can submit a PDF, JPG, or PNG invoice (up to 8 MB) with an amount. The planner can download the file and update its status from the event page.</p>
</section>

<section class="learning-finish">
  <div><p class="eyebrow">Ready when you are</p><h2>Bring your event details together.</h2><p>Start with one event and invite one vendor to try the flow.</p></div>
  <a class="button primary" href="<%= user ? '/dashboard' : '/auth' %>"><%= user ? 'Go to dashboard' : 'Create your account' %> <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
</section>
<%- include('partials/foot') %>
